Now I have a clear picture. Let me look at the Go visibility logic more carefully — Go uses capitalization for public/private. Ruby treats things starting with _ as private. Shell treats everything as public. Let me understand the nuance of each:

• Go: `is_public = name.starts_with(|c: char| c.is_uppercase())`
• Ruby: Classes/modules/consts always is_public: true; functions: `!name.starts_with('_')`
• Shell: Always is_public: true

